{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfumKY5yUbdjoJ4UpbtwK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the `--retry` option's sibling, `--repeats`, no wait, the right one is the `repeats` test option, which the CLI exposes as `--repeats`:\n\n```\nnpx vitest run --repeats=10\n```\n\nHmm, to be accurate: Vitest's CLI has `--retry=<n>` (reruns a test only after it fails), and the \"run each test N times\" behavior is the `repeats` option, which is set per test or suite (`test('name', { repeats: 10 }, () => {})` or `it.repeats`-style options), not reliably as a global CLI flag. I'm not certain a `--repeats` CLI flag exists in your version, so check `npx vitest --help`.\n\nPractical approaches that work regardless:\n\n- **Per test/suite:** `test('foo', { repeats: 20 }, () => { ... })` runs it 20 times and fails if any run fails (Vitest also runs `--retry` separately).\n- **Whole suite from the shell (PowerShell):** `1..20 | ForEach-Object { npx vitest run; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { break } }`\n- **Surface order-dependent flakiness:** add `--sequence.shuffle` so each run uses a different test order.\n\nRetries (`--retry=3`) help tolerate flakiness but hide it, so use them for mitigation, not detection."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2250,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2250},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37280a95-1613-4d2b-8aaa-b95476a2cb4c","uuid":"acbae1f6-97f6-4596-b4e0-da38dc3aee04","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:47:35.785Z","request_id":"req_011CfumKXtZvpbsbfGKSi3k8"}
